{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-8476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the equation $3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\sqrt{3}=0$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ Given that the exact solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ and ${x}_{4}$ are written in ascending order, what is the value of ${x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-8476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\sqrt{3} & =0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6} & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{n\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(3n+1)\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{2\\pi }{3},\\frac{7\\pi }{6},\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${x}_{2}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ and ${x}_{3}=\\frac{7\\pi }{6},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}\\cdot \\frac{7\\pi }{6}=\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{9}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-8476" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6daf4b6401d655f378666147403cd8fd8ec23c94571f7755738dcf6e123ca897"} {"question" "q-8476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-8476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{7\\pi }{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{9\\pi }{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-8476" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{9}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-8477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})=1$ for $0\\le x<\\pi .$ If the exact solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are written in ascending order, what is the value of ${x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-8477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-\\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ 3x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(2n+1)\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$ So, the solutions ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4}$ (written in ascending order) are\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and ${x}_{3}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{6}=\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{12}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-8477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6daf4b6401d655f378666147403cd8fd8ec23c94571f7755738dcf6e123ca897"} {"question" "q-8477" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-8477" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{12}"] ["math" "-\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\pi }{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{12}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-8477" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5{\\pi }^{2}}{12}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-8559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the exact solutions to the equation $\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3})+\\sqrt{3}=0$ for $0\\le x<\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-8559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange the equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3})+\\sqrt{3}=0 \\\\  & \\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3})=-\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & \\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3})=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{7\\pi }{3} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =\\frac{7\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{25\\pi }{12}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{25\\pi }{24}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2} \\\\ x & =\\frac{(12n+25)\\pi }{24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=-2$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24}$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=\\frac{13\\pi }{24}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $0\\le x<\\pi .$ So, the solutions are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{24},\\frac{13\\pi }{24}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{24}\\cdot \\frac{13\\pi }{24}=\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-8559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6daf4b6401d655f378666147403cd8fd8ec23c94571f7755738dcf6e123ca897"} {"question" "q-8559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-8559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{24}"] ["math" "-\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}"] ["math" "\\frac{13\\pi }{24}"] ["math" "\\frac{13\\pi }{576}"] ["math" "\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-8559" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{13{\\pi }^{2}}{576}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-65851" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the exact solutions to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=1$ for $-2\\pi \\le x<2\\pi ,$ what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-65851" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the equation above for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{(4n+1)\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain $-2\\pi \\le x<2\\pi .$\n\n- Setting $n=-1$ gives $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain $-2\\pi \\le x<2\\pi .$ So, the solutions are $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}=-\\pi .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-65851" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6daf4b6401d655f378666147403cd8fd8ec23c94571f7755738dcf6e123ca897"} {"question" "q-65851" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-65851" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "-\\pi "] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-65851" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\pi "] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-274701" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Expressed in **ascending order** in degrees, the **exact solutions** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x-{90}^{∘})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$  are\n\n${x}_{1}=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{3}=$\n{{field-3}}${}^{∘},\\,{x}_{4}=$\n{{field-4}}${}^{∘}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-274701" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We will find the general solution to the equation, and then generate all of the solutions in the required domain.\n\nThe general solution to our equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & ={60}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving our equation for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={30}^{∘}+n\\cdot {90}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe set $n=0,\\pm 1,\\pm 2,…,$ until we have generated all solutions in the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$\n\n- Setting $n=0$ gives $x={30}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=1$ gives $x={120}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=2$ gives $x={210}^{∘}$\n\n- Setting $n=3$ gives $x={300}^{∘}$\n\nAll other values of $n$ generate solutions outside the domain ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘}.$ \n\nSo, the solutions to the equation, in ascending order, are \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}={30}^{∘},\\,{x}_{2}={120}^{∘},\\,{x}_{3}={210}^{∘},\\,{x}_{4}={300}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/state.json" "file_sha256" "1d74d261d2e3535e173c0d08beb165a31e769733a1ee187750319c56c306c1b2"} {"question" "q-274701" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990828/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6daf4b6401d655f378666147403cd8fd8ec23c94571f7755738dcf6e123ca897"} {"question" "q-274701" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/ja